title A guard that refuses and blames the wrong file
prompt Baton -- open the round, read the rota, take the next auditing lap.
think rota lap 3985, row 0 -- Aether by the modulus, the row that hears, unread since lap 3949. Read the threshold and its triad: follow-our-compass, the Lindy effect, the grain and the crossing. The strand at the fusion is the one that steered the lap -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything.
think Reds first found nothing agent-closable in this lane: %431 sits at custody gate %1 and %360's remainder is named to other lanes. So the constructive queue was open, and the card had already hoisted one sentence out of a yonder design and marked it as the part that should not wait -- a guard that cannot run its instrument refuses, and says which instrument. Aether's instruction is to ask what the work is saying underneath the words, so I asked whether the tree already obeyed its own hoisted sentence rather than assuming it did.
think Measured rather than reasoned. My first regex for rg call sites counted comments and reported six roster-reachable scripts; three of those were files documenting the elder pattern in prose. Stripping full-line comments and requiring command position read 1,351 sites across 126 files, and a transitive walk of the roster's 1,503 reachable scripts found exactly three that reach rg where it runs.
think Then the metal reading, which is the only part that mattered: removed the one PATH entry holding rg, changed nothing else, and ran all three. Every one refused. Not one named the tool.
think Checked each accusation with plain grep before writing a word of it. tally/parse_int.rye carries LeadingZero and InvalidCharacter twice each; src/gate/shape-tally-max-gardens.glow is present and matches; e122's control had printed verdict=ok one line above the gate that called it failed. Three false accusations, checked from the other side.
think Sized the repair by what each site could honestly do. Two Tally witnesses reach for one pattern apiece where grep and find are exact, so they take the fallback and are GREEN with rg and without it. e122 asks twenty-three questions through rg, so it takes ONE require_tool at its door -- cheaper and truer than twenty-three fallbacks written by hand, and it touches no equinox semantics, which is not this seat's lane.
obs THE ACCUSATION IS THE FINDING. All three guards refuse, which is correct behavior, and a lap could stop there and call the tree healthy. What each one then says is a specific, checkable, false claim about a specific innocent file. The one true line -- rg: command not found -- goes to stderr, and a witness reading run output does not keep stderr. So the reading a hand actually receives points at the wrong file with full confidence.
obs This is REDS %240 stood on its head, and that is why no meter here could see it. That one was a wrong zero that read as health; this is a correct refusal that reads as a defect somewhere else. shell_dialect counts GNU-only idioms and finds nothing, because rg -q is not a dialect of anything -- it is a different program. A tree taught to distrust silence had not been taught to distrust noise.
obs THE CONTROL CAUGHT MY OWN LEG, the second lap running. I wrote the last leg to strip the ripgrep PATH entry by directory name, /ripgrep-*/bin, and it SKIPPED on this pier, where the Nix store prefixes that name with a hash. A skip is what a vacuous pass looks like from outside, which is the precise fault this control family was booked for -- so the leg proving the repair was itself the shape the file exists to refuse. It reads the entries that actually hold an executable rg now, which works on any bench.
obs Proven from both sides rather than in the passing direction alone: planting the elder shape back into e122 reds two legs and the control exits behavior_missed. Without that plant the leg could not be told from a bypass.
obs The witness pinned pass=32 and the control now reads 47, so the pin moved by hand with its reasoning written beside it. That is the borrowed-number class %341 and %357 already booked, and the answer is that a pinned count is deliberate: it refuses a leg quietly disappearing.
obs Stale claims swept where I was already standing: two tracked comments read "this pier ships no ripgrep" and ripgrep arrived on 20260905. The correction is the sharper sentence anyway -- a helper that only reads right on the bench which happens to lack a tool is not a portable helper.
obs What I did NOT build, and why: the three tiers, the tool-grant roster, and the meter stay in yonder. The design argues the roster must precede the meter, and the roster is a seat rather than a lap. The design's own Status line now says which half landed, accreted as a dated note rather than rewritten, the way follow-our-compass records its own passes.
loom roster_reachable_scripts=1503 rg_command_sites=1351 rg_files=126 roster_reachable_rg_guards=3 false_accusations_checked=3 control_pass_before=32 control_pass_after=47 planted_legs_red=2
file tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh have_tool and require_tool -- the reflex, refusing at 127 on stdout with the instrument named
file tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable_control.sh fifteen legs, both sides, the last running the real e122 scan with rg taken off PATH
file tools/s/shell_dialect_witness.rish the pinned behavior count 32 -> 47 with its reasoning beside it
file tools/fixtures/e/equinox_e122_roots_bench_kinds_scan.sh one require_tool at the door covering twenty-three rg sites, prove-red still runs
file tools/t/tally_glow_tend_limb1_witness.rish find plus grep for rg --glob; GREEN with and without ripgrep
file tools/t/tally_glow_tend_limb4_witness.rish grep for rg -q, matching the two lines already around it
